\begin_body

\begin_layout Standard
Don’t compare raw Alice/Bob timetags directly but treat them as two independent clocks.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Use this model:
 
\begin_inset Formula $t_{B}\approx a+b\,t_{A}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
where a is the offset and b is the clock-rate drift.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For short files 
\begin_inset Formula $b≈1$
\end_inset

,
 for long runs,
 estimate it.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Practical method
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
1.
 Make a time-difference histogram
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
For many Alice tags 
\begin_inset Formula $A_{i}$
\end_inset

 find nearby Bob tags 
\begin_inset Formula $B_{j}$
\end_inset

 and histogram 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta t=B_{j}-A_{i}$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

The true synchronization offset appears as a sharp coincidence peak.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

This is the standard way to align photon timetag streams.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

NIST-related timing work also describes using coincidence peaks / offsets for alignment.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Find the peak
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Suppose the peak is at 
\begin_inset Formula $\Delta t=\tau$
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Then initially synchronize by using 
\begin_inset Formula $B'_{j}=B_{j}-\tau$
\end_inset

 or equivalently compare 
\begin_inset Formula $A_{i}$
\end_inset

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $B_{j}-\tau$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Apply coincidence window
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

After correction,
 accept a pair when 
\begin_inset Formula $|B_{j}-\tau-A_{i}|<W$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

where (W) might be a few ns or tens of ns,
 etc.
 depending on detector jitter and data resolution.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Check for drift
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Split the run into chunks,
 e.g.
 100 chunks.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

For each chunk,
 find the best 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau_{k}$
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

If 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau_{k}$
\end_inset

 changes linearly with time fit 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau(t)=\tau_{0}+dt$
\end_inset

 then correct Bob by 
\begin_inset Formula $B'_{j}=B_{j}-\tau(B_{j})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Only then compute correlations
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Once the event pairs are formed,
 attach Alice/Bob settings and outcomes to each matched coincidence.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

A simple diagnostic:
 before synchronization the histogram of (B-A) looks flat/noisy;
 after finding the correct offset there should be a clear narrow peak.
 If no peak appears,
 likely causes are wrong timetag units,
 wrong channel extraction,
 large drift,
 or comparing different runs/files.
\end_layout

